<title>EGYPT: Egypt oils firm halves dividend in 95/6.</title>
<headline>Egypt oils firm halves dividend in 95/6.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Extracted Oils and Derivatives almost halved its annual dividend to 2.50 pounds a share for the financial year 95/6 from 4.48 pounds in the previous year, the firm said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The years end on June 30.</p>
<p>Reuters quoted brokers late last month as saying the company would distribute 2.625 pounds a share.</p>
<p>The partially privatised company makes cooking oil, margarine, soap, animal feed and detergents.</p>
<p>$1=3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
